            <ArticleTitle>Coronary angioplasty for congenital obstruction of the left main coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11748-014-0403-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present three children who underwent coronary angioplasty for the surgical treatment of a congenital obstruction of the left main coronary artery. An azygos vein patch or graft was a feasible and useful material for reconstructing congenital ostial stenosis and atresia of the left main coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
